#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Feature-agent prompts for one coverage wave.

    wave-prompts.py <wave-dir> <suffix>

Writes <wave-dir>/prompt-<agent>.txt for each agent in OWNS. Edit OWNS
(one line per agent: what it owns, shown to every agent) and EXTRA (the
agent's own priorities) per wave; the agent names must match the table
in wave-lists.py. <suffix> is appended to branch names so they do not
clash with an earlier wave's branches.
"""
import sys

W, SUF = sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2]
OWNS = {
    'template': 'the template author (`crates/mtg-cards/src/author.rs`) and the phrases it needs: cards whose draft fails to parse or renders with a mismatch, regular sentences the author still skips although the card language can say them, and making the compiler reject the wrong-meaning forms in `KNOWN-ISSUES.md` section 2',
    'transform': 'double-faced and becoming: "exile this, then return it to the battlefield transformed", "when this transforms into", "can\'t transform", "transformed permanent" filters, "becomes a copy of" forms, land animation ("becomes a 3/3 creature that\'s still a land", the Zendikon Auras), and "a spell that\'s both white and black"',
    'mana': 'mana: restricted mana of more than one symbol or added by an effect ("Add two mana in any combination of colors. Spend this mana only to ..."), "Add X mana of any one color, where X is ...", "when you spend this mana to cast ..." riders, counts and conditions on the mana spent to cast a spell, and mana abilities with a non-tap cost that wrongly use the stack',
    'counters-costs': 'counters (kinds, moving, removing, "for each counter", enters-with forms) and costs (additional and alternative costs, taxes, "unless its controller pays", sacrifice and discard costs) still reported missing',
    'zones': 'graveyard, exile, library and hand forms (cast or play from another zone, linked exile, look at / reveal / search forms, mill) and copying of spells and permanents not owned by `transform`',
    'rules': 'combat, triggers, replacement and prevention effects, conditions, counts, targets, durations and static abilities still reported missing, and anything no other agent owns',
}
EXTRA = {
    'template': '''Last wave this work yielded more cards than any other, and the template author costs nothing to run afterwards, so every form it learns pays in all three pools. In order: (1) the parse failures and mismatches on your list, grouped by the phrase that fails (the list is sorted Pauper first; `author --format <f> --verbose` reproduces it); (2) the commonest `sentence:` skip reasons in `{W}/backlog-ranked.tsv` that are only a template or phrase away (not ones another agent owns below); (3) make the author stop writing cards known to be wrong. For (3): for each form in `KNOWN-ISSUES.md` section 2 either bind it correctly or make the compiler reject it, so neither the author nor a card agent can pass the gate with it; and make the author skip, with a reason, what the lead dropped by hand last wave: a spell with five or more modes (Sublime Epiphany, Casualties of War), a battle (Invasion of Lorwyn), a meld pair whose result needs a rule that is missing (Gisela, the Broken Blade), a draft that does not compile (Ravager's Mace), and the two forms behind Deputy of Detention and Grief Tyrant (both in `KNOWN-ISSUES.md`). After each change run the author on all three formats and verify each newly written card with a scenario before adding it (do not run `--write` over a whole format).''',
    'transform': '''In order of cards unlocked: (1) "exile this, then return it to the battlefield transformed [under your control / under its owner's control]" as a Saga's last chapter, an activated ability, and a dies trigger (CR 712; the card returns as a new object with its back face up); (2) "when this permanent transforms into <name>" and "enters or transforms into" triggers; (3) "can't transform", "transform <a chosen permanent>", the "transformed permanent" filter; (4) "a spell that's both white and black" (the Shadowmoor Mimics, Pauper); (5) land animation wording and the Zendikon Auras ("Enchanted land is a 4/2 red Beast creature with trample. It's still a land.", then the land returns to its owner's hand when it dies); (6) "becomes a copy of" forms on your list.''',
    'mana': '''The mana pool is on the hot path of every game: keep `ManaPool` and payment as cheap as they are when no card in the game makes restricted mana (a pool- or state-level flag, not a per-payment scan), and check `hot_structs_stay_small` still passes. In order: (1) restricted mana of several symbols or produced by an effect (about 40 cards; this needs the pool to carry a restriction per unit of mana, not one per ability: design that first, CR 106.6); (2) mana abilities with a non-tap cost must not use the stack (CR 605.3; `KNOWN-ISSUES.md` section 1: Grinning Ignus, Molt Tender); (3) "Add X mana of any one color, where X is ..."; (4) counts and conditions on "the amount of mana spent to cast" a spell and "for each color of mana spent"; (5) "when you spend this mana to cast ..." riders. Compare `target/release/mtg sim --deck1 random:3 --deck2 random:4 --games 500 --seed 5` before and after: the `wins` line must not change.''',
    'counters-costs': '''Your list is long. Do not try every card: read it, group the reports by what is missing, and build the groups in order of Pauper plus Standard cards unlocked. Stop when the remaining groups unlock fewer than about three cards each.''',
    'zones': '''Your list is very long (most of it Modern cards the template author skips at a library or graveyard sentence). Work the Pauper and Standard lines: read them, group by what is missing, and build the groups in order of cards unlocked; teach the template author each regular sentence so the Modern lines follow without your writing them. Also on your list of bugs (`KNOWN-ISSUES.md` section 1): Pigment Wrangler's copy trigger never fires, and the engine makes Thirst for Knowledge's discard choice for the player. Stop when the remaining groups unlock fewer than about three cards each.''',
    'rules': '''Your list has the most Pauper cards, and Pauper is the first coverage target (it needs about 270 more cards for 95%). Do not try every card: read the Pauper lines, then the Standard ones, group the reports by what is missing, and build the groups in order of cards unlocked, Pauper first. Stop when the remaining groups unlock fewer than about three cards each. A count used in a static ability must work in the layer system too (`per_count` in `crates/mtg-core/src/layers.rs` must read `Work`, never `GameState::characteristics`: a debug build panics on re-entry), and `CountExpr::in_static` must classify every count you add.''',
}
for k in OWNS:
    o = '\n'.join(f'- {n}: {d}' + (' (you)' if n == k else '') for n, d in OWNS.items())
    b = f'feature-{k}{SUF}'
    p = f"""You are a feature agent on a Rust Magic: The Gathering rules engine. Your worktree may have been created from an old commit: first run `git checkout -B {b} main` so you start from current main (if git refuses because the branch is checked out in another worktree, use `{b}-b` and say so). Then read `scripts/coverage/feature-brief.md` in your working directory (your git worktree) and follow it exactly. Your notes file (see its section on known issues) is `{W}/notes-{k}.md`.

YOUR ASSIGNMENT (branch name `{b}`): {OWNS[k]}.

{EXTRA[k].replace('{W}', W)}

Your card list is `{W}/lists/{k}.tsv` (card name, formats, and what a card-authoring agent or the template author reported, Pauper cards first, then Standard; a card may need other things too: skip those and say which). Many lines are from earlier waves and may work now. `cargo run -q --release -p mtg-cards -- author --format pauper --verbose` (and `standard`, `modern`; give the modern run a long timeout) lists skipped cards with reasons. Where the wording is regular, add a template to `crates/mtg-cards/src/author.rs`. Do not add the cards named in `{W}/batches/all.txt`: card agents are writing those on main.

OTHER AGENTS working in parallel own these; do not build your own version of any of them, skip cards needing them and say so:
{o}
- four card-authoring agents are adding new card files under `cards/` and `scenarios/agents/` on main

A card counts only if the gate says Match AND a scenario shows it behaves as the Oracle text says, checking amounts and targets. If a form gates Match but means the wrong thing, do not add the card; put it in your notes file under `New`.
Each new form needs DSL syntax, exact Oracle rendering, SYNTAX.md, and scenarios.

Merge hazards: if you take a free bit (`DefFlags`, `GameObject::marks`, `CastInfo`) or add a `Keyword` (`Keyword::ALL` has a fixed length) or a `CounterKind` (`CounterKind::NAMED` has a fixed length), say so in your final reply, since another branch may take the same one. If you add a variant to an enum that is matched exhaustively elsewhere (`CountExpr`, `Effect`, `Trigger`) or change a function's signature, say so too. A new way to cast a card from hand must be added to the list behind `CardDef::other_casts` in `CardPool::add`. You may add a line form to the scenario runner (`crates/mtg-scenario`) if a card cannot be tested without it; do not change what an existing line does, and name the addition in your final reply. Throughput matters: a check you add to a hot path (priority, state-based actions, `characteristics`, every event) must cost nothing when no card in the game uses the feature (gate it on a pool- or state-level flag rather than scanning the battlefield).

Commit as you go (one commit per feature or bug). Write each commit message to a file and commit with `git commit -F <file>`. End each commit message with `Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`. Before your last commit run `cargo fmt`, `cargo clippy -q --workspace`, the gate, the scenarios (release, and once with a debug build: `cargo build -p mtg-cli && target/debug/mtg scenario`), and `timeout 2400 cargo test --workspace` (it includes a format/parse round-trip over the whole corpus). Wrap every cargo test run in `timeout`. When you wait for a background command, never poll with `pgrep -f "<its command line>"`: that matches the polling shell itself and never ends; wait on the command's exit instead. Delete your worktree's `target/` when everything is committed. Final reply: branch name, commit hashes, what you implemented, number of cards added per item, anything left out, bits, keywords, counter kinds, enum variants or signatures you took or changed, and any ENGINE BUG you found."""
    open(f'{W}/prompt-{k}.txt', 'w').write(p)
    print(k, len(p))
